/id #uuid "aa63a6a8-e732-5c46-9e84-c078fc19694e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["answer-ed9c8ce6-3232-550b-ba3e-f1ef8a153d5c" "answer-b51b3ed9-9a4c-55ff-b4f4-f843fff3a90f" "answer-052d61ab-849c-5821-a4c8-7b7df8edf4c1" "answer-55b61929-4b61-58a3-9a39-f15a57582729" "answer-2578a4c9-baea-5075-b13a-e3ee4b4cf98b"] :answer-field/correct "answer-ed9c8ce6-3232-550b-ba3e-f1ef8a153d5c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "question-77c74a84-122e-5dd7-b170-e7f0507d8abe" :question/id #uuid "77c74a84-122e-5dd7-b170-e7f0507d8abe" :question/problem "Assume $x,y,z>0$.\n\n$\\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{2}}{z^{4}}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "The laws of logarithms are:\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(a\\right)+\\log_{n}\\left(b\\right)=\\log_{n}\\left(ab\\right)$ — the product rule\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(a\\right)-\\log_{n}\\left(b\\right)=\\log_{n}\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)$ — the quotient rule\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(c^{m}\\right)=m\\log_{n}\\left(c\\right)$ — the power rule\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{2}}{z^{4}}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{5}\\left(\\sqrt{x}y^{2}\\right)-\\log_{5}\\left(z^{4}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{5}\\left(\\sqrt{x}y^{2}\\right)-\\log_{5}\\left(z^{4}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{5}\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\right)+\\log_{5}\\left(y^{2}\\right)-\\log_{5}\\left(z^{4}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power rule for logarithms (a square root is a power of one half), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{5}\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\right)+\\log_{5}\\left(y^{2}\\right)-\\log_{5}\\left(z^{4}\\right) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{2}\\log_{5}\\left(x\\right)+2\\log_{5}\\left(y\\right)-4\\log_{5}\\left(z\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{2}}{z^{4}}\\right) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{2}\\log_{5}\\left(x\\right)+2\\log_{5}\\left(y\\right)-4\\log_{5}\\left(z\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese identities hold for $x,y,z>0$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["field-aa63a6a8-e732-5c46-9e84-c078fc19694e"] :db/ensure :question/validate} [:db/add 17592186054625 :knowledge-point/questions "question-77c74a84-122e-5dd7-b170-e7f0507d8abe"] {:db/id "answer-dd53ded7-13c1-57b4-b825-b7134085bffc" :answer/id #uuid "dd53ded7-13c1-57b4-b825-b7134085bffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\log\\left(y\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log\\left(x\\right)-5\\log\\left(z\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-3da21178-4f1e-5858-beb5-b49b6e6a77b0" :answer/id #uuid "3da21178-4f1e-5858-beb5-b49b6e6a77b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\log\\left(y\\right)-\\frac{1}{2}\\log\\left(x\\right)-5\\log\\left(z\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-1fb9396d-bfad-59f6-89c3-d2acf5e26d22" :answer/id #uuid "1fb9396d-bfad-59f6-89c3-d2acf5e26d22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\log\\left(y\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log\\left(x\\right)+\\log\\left(z\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-cd018f9d-a675-507c-b3b9-0b17ca7a2512" :answer/id #uuid "cd018f9d-a675-507c-b3b9-0b17ca7a2512" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\log\\left(y\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log\\left(x\\right)-\\log\\left(z\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-290a1a96-bd40-5c3a-8884-19b33e0944ba" :answer/id #uuid "290a1a96-bd40-5c3a-8884-19b33e0944ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\log\\left(y\\right)-\\frac{1}{2}\\log\\left(x\\right)-\\log\\left(z\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "field-bc84df8d-7b1c-57bb-831f-bc0b1a17bb7a" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc84df8d-7b1c-57bb-831f-bc0b1a17bb7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd53ded7-13c1-57b4-b825-b7134085bffc" "answer-3da21178-4f1e-5858-beb5-b49b6e6a77b0" "answer-1fb9396d-bfad-59f6-89c3-d2acf5e26d22" "answer-cd018f9d-a675-507c-b3b9-0b17ca7a2512" "answer-290a1a96-bd40-5c3a-8884-19b33e0944ba"] :answer-field/correct "answer-dd53ded7-13c1-57b4-b825-b7134085bffc" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "question-f3842e0a-970a-5ffe-87fc-38911ec62602" :question/id #uuid "f3842e0a-970a-5ffe-87fc-38911ec62602" :question/problem "Assume $x,y,z>0$.\n\n$\\log\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{3}}{z^{5}}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "The laws of logarithms are:\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(a\\right)+\\log_{n}\\left(b\\right)=\\log_{n}\\left(ab\\right)$ — the product rule\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(a\\right)-\\log_{n}\\left(b\\right)=\\log_{n}\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)$ — the quotient rule\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(c^{m}\\right)=m\\log_{n}\\left(c\\right)$ — the power rule\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{3}}{z^{5}}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log\\left(\\sqrt{x}y^{3}\\right)-\\log\\left(z^{5}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log\\left(\\sqrt{x}y^{3}\\right)-\\log\\left(z^{5}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log\\left(y^{3}\\right)+\\log\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\right)-\\log\\left(z^{5}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power rule for logarithms (a square root is a power of one half), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log\\left(y^{3}\\right)+\\log\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\right)-\\log\\left(z^{5}\\right) \\\\ &= 3\\log\\left(y\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log\\left(x\\right)-5\\log\\left(z\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{3}}{z^{5}}\\right) \\\\ &= 3\\log\\left(y\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log\\left(x\\right)-5\\log\\left(z\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese identities hold for $x,y,z>0$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["field-bc84df8d-7b1c-57bb-831f-bc0b1a17bb7a"] :db/ensure :question/validate} [:db/add 17592186054625 :knowledge-point/questions "question-f3842e0a-970a-5ffe-87fc-38911ec62602"] {:db/id "answer-31ff3f62-3ba2-5b49-853c-80c0366eae50" :answer/id #uuid "31ff3f62-3ba2-5b49-853c-80c0366eae50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-8d51198c-1fa4-56fc-93f9-3b2c9e1fa1fc" :answer/id #uuid "8d51198c-1fa4-56fc-93f9-3b2c9e1fa1fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\log_{3}\\left(2x\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-8abc978f-e039-5d30-85a4-0ba2781112b5" :answer/id #uuid "8abc978f-e039-5d30-85a4-0ba2781112b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\log_{3}\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-cd3bfc25-b686-56dd-b90f-702842f2c361" :answer/id #uuid "cd3bfc25-b686-56dd-b90f-702842f2c361" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\log_{3}\\left(4x\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-e5d37cf2-4ba3-579f-8bc2-9d13decb970f" :answer/id #uuid "e5d37cf2-4ba3-579f-8bc2-9d13decb970f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\log_{3}\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "field-a46c3755-7eae-536c-bcdc-98a79dbadf22" :answer-field/id #uuid "a46c3755-7eae-536c-bcdc-98a79dbadf22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["answer-31ff3f62-3ba2-5b49-853c-80c0366eae50" "answer-8d51198c-1fa4-56fc-93f9-3b2c9e1fa1fc" "answer-8abc978f-e039-5d30-85a4-0ba2781112b5" "answer-cd3bfc25-b686-56dd-b90f-702842f2c361" "answer-e5d37cf2-4ba3-579f-8bc2-9d13decb970f"] :answer-field/correct "answer-8d51198c-1fa4-56fc-93f9-3b2c9e1fa1fc" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "question-41bba485-231e-5eaa-99c4-61446cde6137" :question/id #uuid "41bba485-231e-5eaa-99c4-61446cde6137" :question/problem "Assume $x>0$.\n\nExpress $3\\log_{3}\\left(2\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right)$ as a single logarithm." :question/worked-solution "Using the power rule for logarithms, rewrite the powered numerical term and evaluate the power:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& 3\\log_{3}\\left(2\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(2^{3}\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(8\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, combine the factors with the same sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{3}\\left(8\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(8x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quotient rule for logarithms and simplifying the numerical factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{3}\\left(8x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(\\frac{8x}{4}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(2x\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& 3\\log_{3}\\left(2\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(2x\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese identities hold for $x>0$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["field-a46c3755-7eae-536c-bcdc-98a79dbadf22"] :db/ensure :question/validate} [:db/add 17592186054625 :knowledge-point/questions "question-41bba485-231e-5eaa-99c4-61446cde6137"] [:db/cas 17592186608363 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186608368 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186608371 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186608372 :question/worked-solution "Using the power rule for logarithms, we can rewrite the terms as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& -2\\log_{2}\\left(x\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log_{2}\\left(z\\right)+3\\log_{2}\\left(y\\right) \\\\ &= -\\log_{2}\\left(x^{2}\\right)+\\log_{2}\\left(\\sqrt{z}\\right)+\\log_{2}\\left(y^{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, we combine the factors with the same sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& -\\log_{2}\\left(x^{2}\\right)+\\log_{2}\\left(\\sqrt{z}\\right)+\\log_{2}\\left(y^{3}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{2}\\left(y^{3}\\sqrt{z}\\right)-\\log_{2}\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quotient rule for logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{2}\\left(y^{3}\\sqrt{z}\\right)-\\log_{2}\\left(x^{2}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{2}\\left(\\frac{y^{3}\\sqrt{z}}{x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& -2\\log_{2}\\left(x\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log_{2}\\left(z\\right)+3\\log_{2}\\left(y\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{2}\\left(\\frac{y^{3}\\sqrt{z}}{x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese identities hold for $x,y,z>0$." "First reorder the terms so the two positive logarithms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& -2\\log_{2}\\left(x\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log_{2}\\left(z\\right)+3\\log_{2}\\left(y\\right) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{2}\\log_{2}\\left(z\\right)+3\\log_{2}\\left(y\\right)-2\\log_{2}\\left(x\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the power rule for logarithms, we can rewrite the terms as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\frac{1}{2}\\log_{2}\\left(z\\right)+3\\log_{2}\\left(y\\right)-2\\log_{2}\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{2}\\left(\\sqrt{z}\\right)+\\log_{2}\\left(y^{3}\\right)-\\log_{2}\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, we combine the factors with the same sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{2}\\left(\\sqrt{z}\\right)+\\log_{2}\\left(y^{3}\\right)-\\log_{2}\\left(x^{2}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{2}\\left(y^{3}\\sqrt{z}\\right)-\\log_{2}\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quotient rule for logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{2}\\left(y^{3}\\sqrt{z}\\right)-\\log_{2}\\left(x^{2}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{2}\\left(\\frac{y^{3}\\sqrt{z}}{x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\frac{1}{2}\\log_{2}\\left(z\\right)+3\\log_{2}\\left(y\\right)-2\\log_{2}\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{2}\\left(\\frac{y^{3}\\sqrt{z}}{x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese identities hold for $x,y,z>0$."] [:db/ensure 17592186608372 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186054625 :knowledge-point/validate]]
